FADE IN:

EXT. BUS STOP — NIGHT #1#

Rain hammers the tin roof. A single streetlight flickers.

ARJUN (30s, soaked, restless) checks his watch.
He looks up the empty road.

MEERA (O.S.)
Arjun.

He turns.

MEERA
(stepping into the light)
You said you would never come back.

ARJUN
I said a lot of things.
  
Most of them were true.

/* An alternate beat we cut:
Arjun laughs. */

[[Check the bus timetable for 1994.]]

CUT TO:

INT. APARTMENT — MORNING

= Meera wakes to an empty flat.

Sunlight. The kettle whistles.

MEERA
Who's there?

ARJUN ^
Just me.

> THE KETTLE SCREAMS <

.FLASHBACK - RAILWAY PLATFORM

!NOBODY MOVES.
The train is already gone.

@McCLANE
Yippee.

~Rain, rain, go away
~Come again another day

>SMASH CUT TO BLACK.

===

INT. POLICE STATION — NIGHT

Arjun enters carrying a pistol. [[prop: replica only]]

FADE OUT.
